### III-A Data Collection

The dataset should cover a large combination of input values with as much as possible small number of samples. To achieve this, we set sinusoidal trajectories with different frequencies. This makes various combination of values for the elements of input vector. Also, five different maneuvers are taken into account, making the trajectories discontinuous to include some hard initial values in the dataset, along with refining the data with more various samples. The system with the controller designed in section [II](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2606.08714v1#S2 "II Sliding Mode Controller Design ‣ Hybrid Neural Network and Conventional Controller Approach for Robust Control of Highly Unstable Systems: Application to Tilt-Rotor Control") is simulated for 200 seconds for each maneuver with a time step of 0.1 seconds, resulting in 10,000 samples. The maneuvers are represented by ([15](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2606.08714v1#S3.E15 "In III-A Data Collection ‣ III Direct Input-Output Training Method for Control ‣ Hybrid Neural Network and Conventional Controller Approach for Robust Control of Highly Unstable Systems: Application to Tilt-Rotor Control")) and detailed in Table [I](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2606.08714v1#S3.T1 "TABLE I ‣ III-A Data Collection ‣ III Direct Input-Output Training Method for Control ‣ Hybrid Neural Network and Conventional Controller Approach for Robust Control of Highly Unstable Systems: Application to Tilt-Rotor Control").

